Prompts: default

Purpose:
  Manage, analyze, classify, and preserve project prompts
  before they become executable work.

Lifecycle:
  RECEIVE > ANALYZE > CLASSIFY > COMPARE > IMPACT > DECIDE > EXECUTE | BACKLOG | ARCHIVE

Directories:
  inbox:
    path: ./inbox
    purpose: Newly received prompts

  active:
    path: ./active
    purpose: Prompts affecting active work

  archive:
    path: ./archive
    purpose: Processed prompts and historical knowledge

  extracted:
    path: ./extracted
    purpose: Useful knowledge extracted from prompts

  conflicts:
    path: ./conflicts
    purpose: Prompt conflicts requiring resolution

Types:
  requirement
  feature
  bug
  architecture
  improvement
  constraint
  skill
  process
  decision
  knowledge
  tech-stack
  role-assignment
  provisioning

Rules:
  [P1] Every new prompt MUST be analyzed before execution.
  [P2] AI MUST check existing prompt knowledge before processing new prompt.
  [P3] A prompt MUST be compared against existing project knowledge.
  [P4] Prompts MUST be archived, not deleted.
  [P5] Prompts MUST be categorized by domain.
  [P6] Tech stack prompts MUST resolve to skill paths.
  [P7] Role assignment prompts MUST require human approval.
  [P8] Provisioning prompts MUST only execute after approval.


State: +

